        "quote": "\t\t\t\tObject value = propertySource.getProperty(key);\n\t\t\t\tif (value != null) {\n\t\t\t\t\tif (resolveNestedPlaceholders) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tif (value instanceof String string) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tvalue = resolveNestedPlaceholders(string);\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\telse if ((value instanceof CharSequence cs) && (String.class.equals(targetValueType) ||\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCharSequence.class.equals(targetValueType))) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tvalue = resolveNestedPlaceholders(cs.toString());\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\tlogKeyFound(key, propertySource, value);\n\t\t\t\t\treturn convertValueIfNecessary(value, targetValueType);\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}",
        "explanation": "Sources are queried in PropertySources iteration order, without consulting containsProperty; the first source whose getProperty(key) returns a non-null raw value wins. A null raw result advances to the next source, and a null source collection or all-null results produce null. Once a non-null raw value is found, nested processing, logging, and conversion occur and the method returns that result—even if conversion returns null—so lower-priority sources are not tried. There is no catch: an exception from a PropertySource or any subsequent processing propagates immediately and also prevents later-source lookup. The resolver does not cache property values or converted results; each lookup scans the current sources again, subject to any caching a custom source may perform itself."
