        "end_line": 283,
        "quote": "\tprotected String resolveNestedPlaceholders(String value) {\n\t\tif (value.isEmpty()) {\n\t\t\treturn value;\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn (this.ignoreUnresolvableNestedPlaceholders ?\n\t\t\t\tresolvePlaceholders(value) : resolveRequiredPlaceholders(value));\n\t}",
        "explanation": "Automatic resolution inside a property value is strict by default because ignoreUnresolvableNestedPlaceholders initially is false; setting it true selects non-strict handling. This nested path returns an empty String unchanged. Independently of that setting, explicit resolvePlaceholders always uses a non-strict helper, while resolveRequiredPlaceholders always uses a strict helper. Explicit empty text is also returned unchanged because the parser finds no placeholder; null text is rejected with IllegalArgumentException. Non-strict mode suppresses only the unresolved-placeholder error by retaining unresolved placeholder text (after any available inline fallback has been considered). It does not suppress circular-reference errors, exceptions from property retrieval/conversion, or other processing exceptions. Strict unresolved and circular cases throw PlaceholderResolutionException."
