        "start_line": 214,
        "end_line": 242,
        "quote": "\t@Override\n\tpublic String getProperty(String key, String defaultValue) {\n\t\tString value = getProperty(key);\n\t\treturn (value != null ? value : defaultValue);\n\t}\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic <T> T getProperty(String key, Class<T> targetType, T defaultValue) {\n\t\tT value = getProperty(key, targetType);\n\t\treturn (value != null ? value : defaultValue);\n\t}\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic String getRequiredProperty(String key) throws IllegalStateException {\n\t\tString value = getProperty(key);\n\t\tif (value == null) {\n\t\t\tthrow new IllegalStateException(\"Required key '\" + key + \"' not found\");\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn value;\n\t}\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic <T> T getRequiredProperty(String key, Class<T> valueType) throws IllegalStateException {\n\t\tT value = getProperty(key, valueType);\n\t\tif (value == null) {\n\t\t\tthrow new IllegalStateException(\"Required key '\" + key + \"' not found\");\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn value;\n\t}",
        "explanation": "Ordinary and typed retrieval are nullable. Default-valued overloads perform the same complete lookup and return the supplied, already typed default only when its final result is null; the default is not converted. Consequently, if a non-null raw value from the winning source is processed or converted to null, lower sources are still skipped but the API default is used. Required overloads perform the same lookup and throw IllegalStateException only when its final result is null, including a null produced after finding a source value. None of these wrappers catches failures: placeholder, source, logging, or conversion exceptions propagate as-is, so neither an API default nor the required-property “not found” exception replaces such a failure."
